{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ECC",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "? and who knoweth the interpretation of a thing? a man's wisdom maketh his face to shine, and the boldness of his face shall be changed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "counsel thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to keep the king's commandment, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in regard of the oath of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not hasty to go out of his sight: stand not in an evil thing; for he doeth whatever pleaseth him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where the word of a king ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " power: and who may say to him, what doest thou?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He who keepeth the commandment shall feel no evil thing: and a wise man's heart discerneth both time and judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because to every purpose there is time and judgment, therefore the misery of man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he knoweth not that which shall be: for who can tell him when it shall be?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no man that hath power over the spirit to retain the spirit; neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "hath he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " power in the day of death: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no discharge in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " war; neither shall wickedness deliver those that are given to it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All this have I seen, and applied my heart to every work that is done under the sun: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a time in which one man ruleth over another to his own hurt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And so I saw the wicked buried, who had come and gone from the place of the holy, and they were forgotten in the city where they had so done: this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " also vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though a sinner doeth evil a hundred times, and his ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "days",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are prolonged, yet surely I know that it will be well with them that fear God, who fear before him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But it will not be well with the wicked, neither will he prolong ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " days, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as a shadow; because he feareth not before God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is a vanity which is done upon the earth; that there are just ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", to whom it happeneth according to the work of the wicked; again, there are wicked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", to whom it happeneth according to the work of the righteous: I said that this also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I commended mirth, because a man hath no better thing under the sun, than to eat, and to drink, and to be merry: for that shall abide with him of his labor the days of his life, which God giveth him under the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done upon the earth: (for also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " neither day nor night seeth sleep with his eyes:)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ECC.8.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ECC.8.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I beheld all the work of God, that a man cannot find out the work that is done under the sun: because though a man may labor to seek ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " out, yet he shall not find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; yes further; though a wise ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thinketh to know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", yet shall he not be able to find ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
